<article class="env-lemma" id="0A2G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A2G">Lemma <span data-tag="0A2G">12.30.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{I}$ be a filtered category. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive, Karoubian category. Let $F : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{A}$ and $G : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{A}$ be functors. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$F \oplus G : \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{A}$ is essentially constant, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$F$ and $G$ are essentially constant. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume (1) holds. In particular $W = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _\mathcal {I} F \oplus G$ exists and hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/0A2F" data-tag="0A2F">12.30.2</a> we have $W = X \oplus Y$ with $X = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _\mathcal {I} F$ and $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _\mathcal {I} G$. A straightforward argument (omitted) using for example the characterization of Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/05PY" data-tag="05PY">4.22.9</a> shows that $F$ is essentially constant with value $X$ and $G$ is essentially constant with value $Y$. Thus (2) holds. The proof that (2) implies (1) is omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>